  "text": "None of the three derivations holds up under checking, so I can only give a low-confidence pick.\n\n- **Solution 2 (3):** The displayed formula is asserted without justification, and the claim that all $(k,l)$-dependence cancels is not argued. The relation $\\chi - 3\\sigma + 48\\,\\mathrm{ind}$ is only a mod-48 identity, so it cannot by itself fix the integer $\\bar\\nu$.\n- **Solution 3 (6):** The parity argument is plausible, but the coboundary step is not justified. It assumes the disc bundle over the flag manifold carries a Spin(7)-extension of the G2-structure, and that is never shown. The intersection-form determinant is asserted rather than computed.\n- **Solution 1 (24):** The claim that the two structures have equal absolute value and opposite signs is the natural shape for this question, since the problem asks for a single $|\\bar\\nu|$. Its derivation is also only a citation sketch. I have a faint recollection that Crowley–Goette–Nordström computed these values, with 24 among them, but I cannot verify that without a source.\n\nI have no tools here to check the Crowley–Goette–Nordström paper, so this choice rests on the structure of the claims rather than a verified value.\n\nCHOICE: 1",
